<code>assert 0 <= index && index <= \old(this.size()) && role != null => this.get(index).equals(role);</code>

This assert statement checks that if the index is within the valid range (0 to the size of the list inclusive) and the role is not null, then the element at the specified index after the insertion is equal to the role that was inserted.
--------------------
<code>assert 0 <= index && index <= \old(this.size()) && role != null => this.get(index).equals(role);</code>

Note: The condition `0 <= index && index <= \old(this.size())` ensures that the index is within the valid range before the insertion. The implication `=>` ensures that if these conditions are met, then the element at the specified index after the insertion is equal to the role being inserted.
